  "body": "The camcraft-mcp skill (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`) has no row for the drawn-cutter MCP tools, although the live registry (`tools::list()`, `crates/app/src/mcp/cutter_tools.rs`) has them:\n\n- `get_tool_cutter_profile` and `set_tool_cutter_profile`, from #93 slice 2 (PR #856, merged);\n- `set_tool_cutter_params {name, diameter?, corner_r?, tip_angle?, flute_len?, shank_d?, shank_len?, neck?: {diameter, length} | null}`, from #93 slice 3 (PR #1012, open, merges at the next cut).\n\nAgents driving CamCraft from the skill won't know they exist. It also matters that, since #852 (PR #957), the drawn neck feeds the collision checks and the simulation (it is no longer display only), so the skill should say so.\n\nThis is a process file, so the fix is its own small PR with a `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` bump. List the slice-2 tools now; add `set_tool_cutter_params` once PR #1012 merges, so the table never names a tool main doesn't have.\n\nDone means: all three tools appear in the skill's tool table with their parameters and undo note, plus the neck-feeds-the-checks note once #957 merges; PROCESS_VERSION bumped; #681 announced on merge.\n",
